From: Project Arctic
Subject: winewayland: a mode the compositor no longer sends is dropped.

The modes of an output were only ever added to: a mode the compositor
stopped sending (dwm.exe's custom refresh rate the user removed, or turned
off with Win+Ctrl+Shift+B) stayed in EnumDisplaySettings until the process
ended, and a program choosing it failed. The list the compositor sends with
each done is the whole list, as wl_output has it, and replaces ours.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_output.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_output.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_output.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_output.c
@@ -139,6 +139,12 @@
 
     if (output->pending_flags & WAYLAND_OUTPUT_CHANGED_MODES)
     {
+        /* The compositor sends the whole list again: a mode it no longer
+         * has (a custom refresh rate removed) goes from ours too. */
+        rb_destroy(&output->current.modes, wayland_output_mode_free_rb, NULL);
+        rb_init(&output->current.modes, wayland_output_mode_cmp_rb);
+        output->current.modes_count = 0;
+        output->current.current_mode = NULL;
         RB_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(mode, &output->pending.modes, struct wayland_output_mode, entry)
         {
             wayland_output_state_add_mode(&output->current,
